00:38:43.140 --> 00:39:01.629
Andy Woodruff: different governance policies. So one example of this will be our revenue splits. So when a payment period is settled, the system will be able to read the splits from GitHub, rather than relying on an admin to enter them manually, or them being hard-coded into the software.

290
00:39:02.710 --> 00:39:17.049
Andy Woodruff: This allows for us to… to have verifiability, specifically when it comes to, key parameters around, the revenue splits and getting people paid,

291
00:39:17.690 --> 00:39:22.129
Andy Woodruff: So… The GitHub Wiki holds everything else.

292
00:39:22.310 --> 00:39:35.079
Andy Woodruff: Our design decisions, implementation guides, and our roadmap. This keeps the official framework clean, while providing rich context for anyone trying to understand the rationale behind our governance choices.

